Section: Development
Homepage: https://muratkurt.github.io/
Description: RootHide compatibility bridge for Claude Code CLI
 Claude Code installs on RootHide but does not work: the Bash tool
 fails with "No suitable shell found", the Read/Write/Edit/Search
 tools cannot resolve paths, and OAuth login never opens Safari.
 The cause is RootHide's concealment architecture - the bootstrap
 toolchain and Claude Code live in different namespaces.
 .
 This package bridges the two. The result: all of Claude Code's
 tools work at FULL CAPABILITY on RootHide.
 .
 Secondary feature: alongside your official Claude account (OAuth),
 you can configure alternative Anthropic-compatible API/gateway
 profiles. Tokens are never embedded in the package; they are stored
 in your home directory with 0600 permissions.
 .
 USAGE:
 claude-rh --original          official Claude account (OAuth)
 claude-provider add <name>    add an alternative API profile
 claude-provider use <name>    set as default
 claude-rh                     launch with the active profile
 claude-rh-doctor              self-test
 .
 NOTE: this package's command is claude-rh. The claude and
 claude-auth commands on your system belong to the
 com.anthropic.claude-code package and do NOT use this bridge.
 .
 REQUIRED: com.anthropic.claude-code must be installed first.
 Get it from:
   https://imcynic.github.io/claude-code-ios/
 .
 On RootHide, Sileo will send this package through RootHide Patcher
 (convert screen) before installing. That is expected, not an error.
