Section: Development
Homepage: https://muratkurt.github.io/
Description: on-device tweak development tools
 Measure the device instead of guessing: class and method lookup from
 the dyld cache, the view tree of a running app or of SpringBoard,
 namespace translation, a Preferences recipe finder, a measurement log
 with a summariser, and an on-device FairPlay decrypt.
 .
 Every tool prints its own usage with --help. Missing dependencies are
 named, not guessed at: node is needed ONLY by shiv-sinif, frida only
 by the tools that attach to a process.
 .
 shiv-kurulum drops the canonical instruction file into a project as
 CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md (it backs up an existing copy first, never
 overwrites it).
 .
 NOTE: the bundled frida client is arm64e, so the frida-backed tools
 (shiv-ekran, shiv-pencere, shiv-oku, shiv-cek, shiv-sinif --tip) need
 an A12 or newer device. shiv-sinif itself does not use frida and works
 everywhere.
 .
 These tools come from shiv; they are packaged separately so any CLI
 can use them.
